            "instructions": "1. Write your current definitions of current and potential difference. 2. Read a short source or watch a short explanation that contrasts them. 3. For a simple series circuit, explain in writing why current is the same everywhere and why potential difference is shared. 4. For a simple parallel circuit, explain why potential difference is the same and current splits. 5. Identify one place where your old confusion would have led to a wrong prediction.",
